<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<LanguageData>

  <!-- Settings: window category (mod-list entry). "melee weapon" follows Core's ThingCategoryDef
       WeaponsMelee ("armas de corpo a corpo"); the unhyphenated form dominates the corpus 56 to 9. -->
  <!-- EN: Unique Melee Weapons -->
  <UMW_SettingsCategory>Armas de corpo a corpo únicas</UMW_SettingsCategory>

  <!-- Settings: section headers. "Trait abilities" heads the tuning of the abilities some weapon
       traits grant (the word "trait" as in weapon trait, the same word as the Traits header). The
       quest section's header is "{0} quest" with {0} the warband faction's def label, capitalized
       and already localized, so it reads "Warband quest"; phrase it so the injected name needs no
       inflection. -->
  <!-- EN: Weapons -->
  <UMW_SettingsWeapons>Armas</UMW_SettingsWeapons>

  <!-- EN: Traits -->
  <UMW_SettingsTraits>Características</UMW_SettingsTraits>

  <!-- EN: Generation -->
  <UMW_SettingsGeneration>Geração</UMW_SettingsGeneration>

  <!-- EN: Traders -->
  <UMW_SettingsTraders>Comerciantes</UMW_SettingsTraders>

  <!-- EN: Trait abilities -->
  <UMW_SettingsTraitAbilities>Habilidades das características</UMW_SettingsTraitAbilities>

  <!-- EN: {0} quest -->
  <UMW_SettingsQuestSection>Missão: {0}</UMW_SettingsQuestSection>

  <!-- EN: Compatibility -->
  <UMW_SettingsCompat>Compatibilidade</UMW_SettingsCompat>

  <!-- EN: The unique weapons that can be generated. A weapon that is turned off will no longer appear as a reward or in loot, and the others will take its place. Weapons already in your save are not affected. A group's box switches the whole group, and a half-filled box means some of its rows are off. Click and drag across rows to switch several at once. -->
  <UMW_SettingsWeaponsDesc>As armas únicas que podem ser geradas. Uma arma desativada deixará de aparecer como recompensa ou na pilhagem, e as outras ocuparão o lugar dela. Armas já existentes no seu jogo salvo não são afetadas. A caixa de um grupo alterna o grupo inteiro, e uma caixa meio preenchida indica que algumas linhas estão desativadas. Clique e arraste pelas linhas para alternar várias de uma vez.</UMW_SettingsWeaponsDesc>

  <!-- EN: The traits that can appear on newly generated unique weapons. A trait that is turned off will no longer appear, and the others will take its place. Weapons that already carry it keep it. Every weapon must keep at least one trait it can start with, so the last one left for a weapon cannot be turned off. A group's box switches the whole group, and a half-filled box means some of its rows are off. Click and drag across rows to switch several at once. -->
  <UMW_SettingsTraitsDesc>As características que podem aparecer em armas únicas recém-geradas. Uma característica desativada deixará de aparecer, e as outras ocuparão o lugar dela. Armas que já a possuem continuarão com ela. Cada arma precisa ter pelo menos uma característica inicial disponível. Por isso, a última que restar para uma arma não pode ser desativada. A caixa de um grupo alterna o grupo inteiro, e uma caixa meio preenchida indica que algumas linhas estão desativadas. Clique e arraste pelas linhas para alternar várias de uma vez.</UMW_SettingsTraitsDesc>

  <!-- EN: Unique melee weapons in trader stock. Every trader is off by default. A trader that can stock them will also buy them, even while its row is off. Weapons turned off in the Weapons section never appear in stock. -->
  <UMW_SettingsTradersDesc>Armas corpo a corpo únicas no estoque dos comerciantes. Todos os comerciantes começam desativados. Um comerciante que pode ter essas armas em estoque também as comprará, mesmo com a linha dele desativada. Armas desativadas na seção Armas nunca aparecerão no estoque.</UMW_SettingsTradersDesc>

  <!-- Settings: reusable label suffixes. Each includes a leading space, and every applicable one is
       appended (no precedence between them), so they must read cleanly back to back. -->
  <!-- EN:  (default) -->
  <UMW_DefaultSuffix> (padrão)</UMW_DefaultSuffix>

  <!-- {0} is another piece of content the current value matches, named from its own def label
       (the ancient-mercenaries site part, "Mercenários Anciões"). Its gender is unknowable here, so
       the suffix reaches it through "a" with no article rather than a contracted "ao/à". -->
  <!-- EN:  (same as {0}) -->
  <UMW_SameAsSuffix> (igual a {0})</UMW_SameAsSuffix>

  <!-- Checkbox-row suffixes, at most one per row, each with a leading space. The first is appended
       to a group header (which is the bare name of a mod or DLC) only while that mod or DLC is not
       installed or not enabled, so the greyed header reads "Royalty (3) (not active)". {0} in the second
       is a weapon's def label (lowercase): the row is a trait that cannot be turned off because it is
       the last trait that weapon could roll first, so the box is held on. -->
  <!-- EN:  (not active) -->
  <UMW_NotActiveSuffix> (inativo)</UMW_NotActiveSuffix>

  <!-- EN:  (last trait for {0}) -->
  <UMW_LastTraitSuffix> (última característica para {0})</UMW_LastTraitSuffix>

  <!-- EN:  (requires restart) -->
  <UMW_RequiresRestartSuffix> (requer reinício)</UMW_RequiresRestartSuffix>

  <!-- Settings: grouped rows. In the Weapons and Traits sections, the rows an optional mod or DLC
       adds sit under a header that is just that mod or DLC's name and its row count (coloured, no
       extra text), with a three-state box that switches the whole group. The first string is the
       count, with a leading space, appended to the name in the name's colour so the header reads
       "Royalty (3)"; {0} is how many weapons or traits this mod adds for that mod or DLC in that
       section, shown even while it is not active. The second is the header's tooltip; {0} is the name,
       injected already coloured: do not inflect it. The last sentence describes click-and-drag
       painting over the checkbox rows beneath the header. -->
  <!-- EN:  ({0}) -->
  <UMW_GroupCountSuffix> ({0})</UMW_GroupCountSuffix>
  <!-- EN: Everything from {0} in this section. -->
  <UMW_IntegrationGroupDesc>Tudo de {0} nesta seção.</UMW_IntegrationGroupDesc>
  <!-- EN: Traits original to {0}. -->
  <UMW_OwnTraitsGroupDesc>Características originais de {0}.</UMW_OwnTraitsGroupDesc>
  <!-- EN: Melee counterparts of the traits {0} gives its unique ranged weapons. -->
  <UMW_OdysseyTraitsGroupDesc>Equivalentes corpo a corpo das características que {0} dá às suas armas à distância únicas.</UMW_OdysseyTraitsGroupDesc>

  <!-- Fallback display names, used only while the mod is not installed. Proper nouns: kept verbatim. -->
  <!-- EN: Vanilla Factions Expanded - Pirates -->
  <UMW_ModNameVfePirates>Vanilla Factions Expanded - Pirates</UMW_ModNameVfePirates>

  <!-- EN: Vanilla Textures Expanded -->
  <UMW_ModNameVte>Vanilla Textures Expanded</UMW_ModNameVte>

  <!-- Settings: Weapons. One checkbox per weapon. {0} is the weapon's own def label (lowercase), whose
       gender varies (machado único / espada longa única) and which nothing inflects for us, so the
       Portuguese never agrees with {0}: it names the subject as "esta arma" once and keeps every later
       reference on that feminine noun. -->
  <!-- EN: Allow {0} to be generated. -->
  <UMW_WeaponEnabledDesc>Permitir a geração desta arma: {0}.</UMW_WeaponEnabledDesc>

  <!-- Settings: Traits. One checkbox per trait. {0} is the trait's own def label (lowercase). -->
  <!-- EN: Allow {0} to appear on newly generated unique weapons. -->
  <UMW_TraitEnabledDesc>Permitir que a característica {0} apareça em armas únicas recém-geradas.</UMW_TraitEnabledDesc>

  <!-- Settings: Generation -->
  <!-- {0} is the wood resource's item label (ThingDef WoodLog, "madeira", lowercase). -->
  <!-- EN: Exclude {0} from generated unique weapons -->
  <UMW_ExcludeWoodStuff>Excluir {0} das armas únicas geradas</UMW_ExcludeWoodStuff>

  <!-- {0} is the vanilla longsword's item label (lowercase), named as the example reward. It is an
       injected label, so the Portuguese reaches it through the vanilla material frame "de madeira"
       (Core's ThingMadeOfStuffLabel is "{1} de {0}") and puts no article in front of it: "na forma de
       {0} de madeira" needs no gender agreement. -->
  <!-- EN: When enabled, unique weapons will never be generated from wood, so a quest reward is never a wooden {0}. When disabled, wood is one of the materials a weapon can be made from. -->
  <UMW_ExcludeWoodStuffDesc>Quando ativado, nenhuma arma única será gerada em madeira, e uma recompensa de missão nunca virá como {0} de madeira. Quando desativado, as armas também podem ser feitas de madeira.</UMW_ExcludeWoodStuffDesc>

  <!-- Settings: Traders. Both toggles default off. The row label is a shared template: {0} is the
       trader kind's own def label, capitalized ("Comerciantes de guerra", "Comerciantes xamãs" -
       vanilla pt-BR renders these TraderKindDef labels as plural nouns even though the English
       source is singular, so the injected value already carries its own agreement); each
       description's {0} is the same label in lowercase, as vanilla already ships it. -->
  <!-- EN: Unique weapons in {0} stock -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniques>Armas únicas em estoque: {0}</UMW_TraderStocksUniques>

  <!-- EN: About half of {0} visits will bring one unique melee weapon of medieval or lower tech level. Ultratech traits never appear on its stock. -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniquesWarMerchantDesc>Cerca de metade das visitas de {0} trará uma arma corpo a corpo única com nível de tecnologia medieval ou inferior. Características ultratecnológicas nunca aparecerão no estoque.</UMW_TraderStocksUniquesWarMerchantDesc>

  <!-- EN: About half of {0} visits will bring one unique melee weapon of medieval or lower tech level. Ultratech traits can appear on its stock, since shamans trade in relics they do not fully understand. -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniquesShamanDesc>Cerca de metade das visitas de {0} trará uma arma corpo a corpo única com nível de tecnologia medieval ou inferior. Características ultratecnológicas podem aparecer no estoque, já que xamãs negociam relíquias que não compreendem totalmente.</UMW_TraderStocksUniquesShamanDesc>

  <!-- Outlander rows, shown only while some unique weapon is of industrial or later make. The
       settlement row's text is fixed (the trader kind has no def label of its own); the caravan and
       trade ship rows add a qualifier because the two combat suppliers share one vanilla label:
       {0} is that label (plural noun phrase, "Comerciantes de combate"), capitalized in the row
       label and lowercase in the description, so it is quoted inside parentheses rather than
       agreed. "forasteiro" is the vanilla outlander term (OutlanderCivil/Rough faction labels,
       "União Forasteira"); medieval / industrial are vanilla's TechLevel names, identical in pt-BR. -->
  <!-- EN: Unique weapons in Outlander settlement stock -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniquesOutlanderSettlement>Armas únicas em estoque: assentamento forasteiro</UMW_TraderStocksUniquesOutlanderSettlement>

  <!-- EN: About one in five outlander settlements will stock one unique melee weapon of industrial or higher tech level. -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniquesOutlanderSettlementDesc>Cerca de um em cada cinco assentamentos forasteiros terá em estoque uma arma corpo a corpo única com nível de tecnologia industrial ou superior.</UMW_TraderStocksUniquesOutlanderSettlementDesc>

  <!-- EN: Unique weapons in {0} caravan stock -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniquesCaravan>Armas únicas em estoque: caravana ({0})</UMW_TraderStocksUniquesCaravan>

  <!-- EN: About one in five {0} caravan visits will bring one unique melee weapon of industrial or higher tech level. -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniquesCaravanDesc>Cerca de uma em cada cinco visitas de caravana ({0}) trará uma arma corpo a corpo única com nível de tecnologia industrial ou superior.</UMW_TraderStocksUniquesCaravanDesc>

  <!-- EN: Unique weapons in {0} trade ship stock -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniquesShip>Armas únicas em estoque: nave comercial ({0})</UMW_TraderStocksUniquesShip>

  <!-- EN: About one in five {0} trade ships will carry one unique melee weapon of industrial or higher tech level. -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniquesShipDesc>Cerca de uma em cada cinco naves comerciais ({0}) trará uma arma corpo a corpo única com nível de tecnologia industrial ou superior.</UMW_TraderStocksUniquesShipDesc>

  <!-- Settings: Trait abilities. Each ability is a subsection headed by its own icon and name (from
       its def, already localized) followed by the first string, which names in parentheses the
       weapon trait that grants it ("Earthshake (Piledriver)"); it has a leading space and {0} is
       that trait's def label, capitalized and already localized. The ability's description is the
       header's tooltip, so the slider rows beneath name only the property: in the next three, {0}
       is the slider's current value. The unit word is part of the template, so hour- and day-based
       cooldowns are separate keys. The last row tunes a different def from the ability above it
       (the rallied buff), so it keeps the subject: {0} is that hediff's def label, capitalized; {1}
       is the value.
       Portuguese keeps the last row's {0} first, as English does, and follows it with a colon.
       Reaching the label through a preposition would want a contracted article ("a duração do
       ânimo"), and the label's gender is unknowable here while nothing in the language worker fuses
       "de" with an article for us. Naming the subject first sidesteps that entirely. -->
  <!-- EN:  ({0}) -->
  <UMW_TraitAbilitySuffix> ({0})</UMW_TraitAbilitySuffix>
  <!-- EN: Cooldown: {0} hours -->
  <UMW_CooldownHours>Tempo de recarga: {0} horas</UMW_CooldownHours>

  <!-- EN: Cooldown: {0} days -->
  <UMW_CooldownDays>Tempo de recarga: {0} dias</UMW_CooldownDays>

  <!-- EN: Radius: {0} cells -->
  <UMW_RadiusCells>Raio: {0} células</UMW_RadiusCells>

  <!-- EN: {0} duration: {1} hours -->
  <UMW_HediffDurationHours>{0}: duração de {1} horas</UMW_HediffDurationHours>

  <!-- {0} is the Odyssey DLC's name, injected already coloured: do not inflect it. -->
  <!-- EN: The time the wielder must wait between earthshakes. The default matches the EMP pulser from {0}. At 0 there is no cooldown. -->
  <UMW_EarthshakeCooldownDesc>O tempo que o usuário precisa esperar entre um tremor de terra e outro. O valor padrão corresponde ao pulsador PEM de {0}. Com 0, não há tempo de recarga.</UMW_EarthshakeCooldownDesc>

  <!-- EN: How far the shockwave reaches. It passes under walls but not across gaps with no floor. A wider radius will catch your own colonists too. -->
  <UMW_EarthshakeRadiusDesc>Até onde a onda de choque alcança. Passa por baixo das paredes, mas não atravessa vãos sem piso. Um raio maior também atingirá seus próprios colonos.</UMW_EarthshakeRadiusDesc>

  <!-- EN: The time the wielder must wait between rallying cries. The default is long enough that a cry stays a rare moment rather than something raised in every fight. -->
  <UMW_RallyingCryCooldownDesc>O intervalo mínimo entre um grito de guerra e outro. O valor padrão é longo o bastante para que o grito continue sendo um momento raro, e não algo usado em todo combate.</UMW_RallyingCryCooldownDesc>

  <!-- EN: How far the cry carries. Everyone in range who is not hostile and can see the wielder will be rallied. Walls block it. Sleepers in range will be woken instead. -->
  <UMW_RallyingCryRadiusDesc>O alcance do grito de guerra. Quem não for hostil e puder ver o usuário ficará enardecido. Paredes bloqueiam o grito. Quem estiver dormindo no alcance apenas acordará.</UMW_RallyingCryRadiusDesc>

  <!-- EN: How long the rallied effect lasts. While it lasts, pain is halved and staggering blows are shaken off twice as fast. -->
  <UMW_RalliedDurationDesc>Quanto tempo dura o efeito do grito de guerra. Enquanto durar, a dor cai pela metade e os golpes fazem cambalear pela metade do tempo.</UMW_RalliedDurationDesc>

  <!-- Settings: Warband quest. The section is headed by the camp's world-map icon and the
       UMW_SettingsQuestSection header above. The first string is that header's tooltip,
       describing the quest; {0} is the Odyssey DLC's name, injected already coloured: do not
       inflect it. "Ancient mercenaries" is the vanilla quest's name; translate it to match the
       official localization. The second is the slider row's label; {0} is the slider's current
       value. The desc's quest examples (ancient mercenaries, bandit camps, item stashes) are
       vanilla content names too. Taken here from the official localization (Odyssey's
       questSubjectRules, Core's BanditCamp and ItemStash SitePartDefs). -->
  <!-- EN: A quest to raid a tribal warband holed up in an abandoned settlement. Their chief carries a unique melee weapon. Capture or kill the chief to take it. It is the low-tech counterpart of the ancient mercenaries quest from {0}. -->
  <UMW_WarbandQuestDesc>Uma missão para atacar um bando de guerra tribal entrincheirado em um assentamento abandonado. O chefe do bando carrega uma arma corpo a corpo única. Capture ou mate o chefe para ficar com ela. É a versão de baixa tecnologia da missão dos mercenários antigos de {0}.</UMW_WarbandQuestDesc>

  <!-- EN: Frequency: {0} -->
  <UMW_QuestCommonality>Frequência: {0}</UMW_QuestCommonality>

  <!-- EN: How often the warband quest is offered compared with similar quests such as ancient mercenaries, bandit camps and item stashes. Higher values offer it more often. At 0 it is never offered. -->
  <UMW_WarbandQuestWeightDesc>Com que frequência a missão do bando de guerra é oferecida em comparação com missões parecidas, como mercenários antigos, acampamentos de bandidos e esconderijos de itens. Valores mais altos farão com que seja oferecida mais vezes. Com 0, nunca será oferecida.</UMW_WarbandQuestWeightDesc>

  <!-- Settings: Compatibility. Shown only when Vanilla Textures Expanded is active. The toggle
       defaults on and is read when the game loads, hence the restart sentence. {0} is our unique
       spear's def label (lowercase); {1} is that mod's display name from its About.xml, injected so
       neither is restated here. Deliberately says nothing about performance. -->
  <!-- EN: Match the {0} to {1} -->
  <UMW_MatchVteSpear>Fazer a {0} corresponder a {1}</UMW_MatchVteSpear>

  <!-- EN: {1} draws the vanilla spear longer and at a diagonal. When enabled, the {0} is turned and enlarged to match it in a drafted pawn's hands. When disabled, it keeps its own size and angle. The change is purely cosmetic and takes effect after a restart. -->
  <UMW_MatchVteSpearDesc>{1} exibe a lança do jogo base mais comprida e na diagonal. Quando ativado, a {0} será girada e aumentada para combinar com essa lança nas mãos de um colono alistado. Quando desativado, manterá o próprio tamanho e ângulo. A mudança é apenas estética e terá efeito depois de reiniciar o jogo.</UMW_MatchVteSpearDesc>

</LanguageData>
